      "body": "## Motivation\n\n#46417 skipped the `CustomAllReduceV2` import on XPU in `dp_attention.py`: `custom_all_reduce_v2` pulls in `tvm_ffi`, which is not in the XPU image, and the module-level import made every XPU launch fail.\n\n`qwen4_decode.py` still has the same module-level import, and after that PR it is the only one left — every other import site is TYPE_CHECKING-guarded or function-lazy. It only fires when a Qwen4-Exp model loads on XPU (qwen4_exp imports it lazily at model init), which is why the XPU CI never saw it, but there it dies the same way:\n\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'tvm_ffi'\n```\n\n## Modifications\n\nThe name moves under TYPE_CHECKING for the annotations, and the two runtime uses import it inside their functions. Both sit behind `prepare_qwen4_decode_comm`'s `not torch.cuda.is_available()` early return, so on XPU (and anywhere without a CUDA device) the import is never executed — the fast path returns None before reaching it.\n\nNo behavior change on CUDA/ROCm: same import, just bound at first use of a cached, called-once constructor.\n\nThis is also the convention the neighboring communication modules (`k3_sp_collective`, `k3_ar_fusion`, `muse_spark_gemm_ag`) already use for this import.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo inference-path change. Ran ruff format, the pre-commit ruff selection, and py_compile locally. No XPU machine on my side, so the XPU claim is import-graph reasoning on top of what #46417 documented for the image.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (import placement only, nothing new to test — happy to add one if wanted)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to the [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (n/a)\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to the [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). (n/a, no inference path change)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidelines](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidelines).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40275863693](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40275863693)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40275863636](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40275863636)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40275863678](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40275863678)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
